## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a robust online ICA system for automotive cabins with real-time constraints and hardware faults.

## Key Concepts
- Online convolutive ICA with dynamic model order
- Robust whitening under missing sensors
- Dropout-aware demixer reinitialization
- Cross-bin permutation continuity across time
- Edge-device latency and evaluation strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: online ICA loop with dropout handling
while (streaming) {
  const frame = readFrame();
  const N = estimateSourceCount(frame);
  whiten(frame, N);
  if (dropoutDetected()) adjustDemixer(N);
  updateDemixer(N);
  alignPermutations(N);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate with synthetic vs real data when ground truth is unavailable?
- Which metrics best reflect real-time separation quality under dropout conditions?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical understanding of online ICA workflow for mobile, real-time audio with nonstationary noise.

## Key Concepts
- Online whitening and demixing; frame-wise updating; permutation alignment.
- Handling nonstationarity; simple energy/phase cues for gating frames.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: simple whitening placeholder (not a full ICA)
function whiten(X) {
  // X: [frames, channels]
  const M = covariance(X);
  const {eigvec, eigval} = eigenDecomp(M);
  return X.dot(eigvec).div(sqrt(eigval));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this to 4 microphones with more moving sources?
- What metrics besides SDR/SIR would help validate perceptual quality?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, end-to-end ICA artifact-removal skills on EEG data, including preprocessing, algorithm choice, artifact identification, and validation with minimal hand‑holding.

## Key Concepts

- EEG referencing and filtering
- Whitening and ICA algorithms (Infomax) suitability for EEG
- Artifact IC identification via EOG correlation, scalp maps, spectral features
- Signal reconstruction and ERP preservation
- Lightweight validation with real and synthetic data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo steps for ICA-based artifact removal (not executable)
const preprocessed = preprocessEEG(raw, {ref: 'CAR', band: [1,40], fsNew: 128})
const whitened = whiten(preprocessed)
const ics = fastICA(whitened, {method: 'infomax'})
const artifactICs = identifyArtifacts(ics, {eog, scalpMaps, emgSpectra})
const cleaned = removeICs(preprocessed, artifactICs)
const validated = validateERP(cleaned, events)
```

